}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{2y-{y}^{2}/2}\\cdot x\\,{|}_{y-2}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-y){e}^{2y-{y}^{2}/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{2y-{y}^{2}/2}\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2(2)-{2}^{2}/2}-{e}^{2(0)-{0}^{2}/2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369516 13194139535840 true] [17592186369515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369517 13194139535840 true] [17592186369515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369518 13194139535840 true] [17592186369515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369519 13194139535840 true] [17592186369515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369520 13194139535840 true] [17592186369515 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535840 true] [17592186369515 1041 "selection" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369515 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369519 13194139535840 true] [17592186369515 1110 #uuid "86f2577b-69b4-5ef6-a518-a4e625baa972" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369516 1034 "2{e}^{2}-1" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369516 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535840 true] [17592186369516 1111 #uuid "f021f72e-8589-5435-931f-dc6a55b09b4f" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369517 1034 "3{e}^{2}-4" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369517 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535840 true] [17592186369517 1111 #uuid "1f2d9100-e583-5f3f-999a-e4d9f3f16c17" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369518 1034 "{e}^{2}+4" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369518 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535840 true] [17592186369518 1111 #uuid "45ff1de4-c070-546e-ac8d-0ab40a47f1f6" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369519 1034 "{e}^{2}-1" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369519 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535840 true] [17592186369519 1111 #uuid "f2b0df37-666c-5efa-ac78-c097ed10555a" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369520 1034 "{e}^{2}+2" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369520 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535840 true] [17592186369520 1111 #uuid "ee1cafa6-5400-5fa8-98b4-e1130e061d21" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369521 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369522 13194139535840 true] [17592186369521 1089 "q-132644" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369521 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535840 true] [17592186369521 1100 "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral \n${\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{\\int }_{-x-3}^{1}6x{e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369521 1113 #uuid "3c73d471-5c90-57d0-8932-12399b90a997" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369521 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/bb17a906727b436562060f84cb1acae42944587cdec6311627e30163485a72d9.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-4\\le x\\le -1,\\,-x-3\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny=-x-3\\,⟹\\,x=-y-3,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=-1.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 1,\\,-y-3\\le x\\le -1},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/f80d088bb764b5dd6aa1c6d26ebd7a5b2a3894c072d81966dec4975fc0e08e59.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{\\int }_{-x-3}^{1}6x{e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{-y-3}^{-1}6x{e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}[{\\int }_{-y-3}^{-1}6x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-y-3}^{-1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}3((-1)^{2}-(-y-3)^{2}){e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}3(1-(y+3)^{2}){e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{3y-(y+3)