e diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/0bed4692a7a6851ef2b66cb3842ebac6b2ef7ef4ff30bed41e84b7cb71c4f5c0.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{3})[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{3})}{4}[{x}^{4}]_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3})]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369558 13194139535840 true] [17592186369557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369559 13194139535840 true] [17592186369557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369560 13194139535840 true] [17592186369557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369561 13194139535840 true] [17592186369557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369562 13194139535840 true] [17592186369557 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535840 true] [17592186369557 1041 "selection" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369557 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369558 13194139535840 true] [17592186369557 1110 #uuid "71092328-12d0-55e5-ac6d-8f789fee8802" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369558 1034 "\\frac{1}{12}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1))" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369558 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535840 true] [17592186369558 1111 #uuid "8ecfd970-b19a-5331-84dc-2e268793a3d6" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369559 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)-1)" 13194139535840 true] [17592186369559 1103 #edb/ref 1759218